<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  android:dataExtractionRules="data_extraction_rules.xml" — the rules that actually GOVERN
  backup and transfer on Android 12+ (API 31+), referenced from <application> in
  AndroidManifest.xml.

  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS ALONGSIDE android:allowBackup="false":
  Google's own wording (https://developer.android.com/guide/topics/data/autobackup,
  "Enable and disable backup") is: "For apps targeting Android 12 (API level 31) or higher,
  this behavior varies. On devices from some device manufacturers, specifying
  android:allowBackup="false" disables cloud-based backup and restore (such as Google Drive
  backups) but doesn't disable device-to-device transfers for the app." So `allowBackup`
  alone leaves D2D transfer to the OEM's interpretation on part of the fleet. This file is
  the mechanism that does NOT vary by manufacturer, so it is what carries the requirement.

  The requirement: nothing this app stores may leave the device by a backup transport. Every
  store is plain JSON on disk — history.json, favorites.json, saved.json, allowlist.json,
  settings.json, customFilters — plus vault.json and the wrapped sync-root blobs, i.e.
  exactly the data this product exists to keep on the user's own device. Sync is the ONLY
  sanctioned way for it to move between a user's own devices, and that goes through this
  app's own encrypted protocol.

  HOW "EVERYTHING" IS EXPRSSED: the rule vocabulary is per-DOMAIN, and `path="."` applies
  recursively to the whole domain. There is no "exclude all" shorthand and no wildcard, so
  every one of the nine domains has to be listed. This list is EXHAUSTIVE against the
  documented domain set (root, file, database, sharedpref, external, device_root,
  device_file, device_database, device_sharedpref) — if Android ever adds a domain, this
  file must gain a line for it, because the platform's own fallback is INCLUSIVE:
  "If there are no rules for a particular backup mode ... that mode is fully enabled for all
  content except for no-backup and cache directories."

  Each of the three sections is listed for the same reason — an absent section is a fully
  enabled one, per that same sentence. <cloud-backup> is Google Drive, <device-transfer> is
  D2D, and <cross-platform-transfer> (Android 16 QPR2 / API 36.1, targetSdk here is 36) is
  the newer hand-off to non-Android devices; a future platform that is not opted out of by
  name would otherwise default to copying everything.

  Note the cache / no-backup / code-cache directories are excluded by the platform whatever
  this file says, so the `root`/`file`/`external` lines here are belt-and-braces for those
  paths rather than the only thing keeping them out.

  There is deliberately NO android:fullBackupContent. That older format is what
  Android 11 (API 30) and lower read, and this app's minSdk is 24 — but `allowBackup="false"`
  already disables the pre-31 cloud path, and the docs say plainly that full-backup-content
  has no effect on D2D transfers on API 31+. A file that looks like it protects the data
  while governing nothing is worse than no file. The pre-31 requirement stays satisfied by
  allowBackup="false"; the API 31+ requirement is met here.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="file" path="." />
        <exclude domain="database" path="." />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="." />
        <exclude domain="external" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_file" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_database" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_sharedpref" path="." />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <exclude domain="root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="file" path="." />
        <exclude domain="database" path="." />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="." />
        <exclude domain="external" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_file" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_database" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_sharedpref" path="." />
    </device-transfer>
    <cross-platform-transfer platform="ios">
        <exclude domain="root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="file" path="." />
        <exclude domain="database" path="." />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="." />
        <exclude domain="external" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_file" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_database" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_sharedpref" path="." />
    </cross-platform-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
